From bed3763fbea89160b94ed0e3ed185cc9d6ba9e22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t2 <t2@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 22:26:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Re-apply the legacy P-scale priority aliases suite update
 6cb0b1e reverted
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

do-work suite update 6cb0b1e (v0.303.8) overwrote the two authorities that
own the Schema Read Contract and the contract table that documents it,
wholesale reverting bca815b. The fourteen do-validate-feedback REQs of
UR-011..UR-015 — which ranked this queue with a finding's severity grade
(`priority: P2`/`P3`/`P4`) before now/next/later existed — went back to
spending a permanent data warning each, putting fourteen lines of noise at
the top of the board in front of the one warning that would matter.

This is the same restore as bca815b, verbatim: the P-scale as read-only
legacy aliases collapsing onto the three canonical bands, in do-work-cli's
schemanormalization and queue-kanban's parser, restated in
work-reference.md's contract table. Nothing writes them back — capture
still emits only the canonical three, and IsCanonicalAuthoringValue stays
false so capture-files keeps refusing to author one.

Verified against the live repository through buildBoard, the seam a real
board read goes through: 0 data warnings, down from 14.

Second time a suite update has reverted this repair; recorded in
docs/imprintwright-v2/DECISIONS.md alongside D-051.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
